
How to set up the server
------------------------

1. Create a Python environment (this step is optional)
My preferred tool to manage Python environments is conda:
conda create -n cgos-server python==3.12.0
conda activate cgos-server

2. Go to directory <server-code>
cd <server-code>

3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

4. Configure cgos19.cfg
You have to decide where on the server the data should be stored.
I will refer to this directory as <server-data>.
Edit cgos19.cfg and replace all occurrences of <server-data> with
your (absolute) path.

5. Create a few directories and an empty database
mkdir logs
mkdir -p <server-data>/19x19
touch <server-data>/19x19/archive.db

6. Copy a few files used for representation of results
mkdir -p <server-data>/public_html/19x19/images
cp cgos/webuild_images/cgosLogo.png <server-data>/public_html/19x19/images

7. Start the Go server
python cgos/server.py cgos19.cfg &

8. Start the website builder
python cgos/webuild.py cgos19.cfg &
Note: You should wait with this until the first match at least has
begun, otherwise the start will fail and you have to restart later.

9. Stop the Go server
touch <server-data>/killCgos19
The kill file is automatically deleted when the server is started again.

